# Signing keys & secrets — NEVER commit these
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.properties
signing.properties
# API credentials. The TMDB key is entered in the app at runtime (Settings -> Metadata ->
# Advanced) and must never reach a build file or the repo; these patterns are the safety net
# for a local scratch copy. The real one for this fork lives in F:\Developing\OwnTV-signing\.
*api-key*.txt
*api_key*.txt
secrets.properties
.env
.env.*

# Internal planning documents — kept local, never committed
future-plan/
audit/

# Upstream triage notebook: which ahXN00/OwnTV and flashingcursor/SteadfastTV commits we take.
# Working notes for this fork only — never pushed.
UPSTREAM_TRIAGE.md

# The PRODUCTION Cloudflare Workers — kept local, never committed.
#
# These are the deployments OwnTV's built-in defaults point at, so they carry abuse protection
# (per-client access checks, request budgets, rate limits) that must not be public: publishing it
# would only tell an abuser exactly how to get around it. Root-scoped so `extras/worker/` — the
# public, unprotected self-host copy users are told to deploy — is NOT caught by this.
/worker/

# i18n seed tool run state (batch inputs, IDs, raw results) — never committed
/runs/


# JVM crash dumps from a Gradle daemon (never worth committing)
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

